// CSD_RATIONALE_BEGIN
// The measured failure source was lack of any produced visible answer span, so
// this revision makes span production the first-class objective instead of
// waiting on broad outside free-text behavior. It preserves the evidence-backed
// ingredients of explicit/observed entry, parser-complete immediate close, and
// mixed symbol/token progress inside the constrained region, but changes one
// causal axis: outside the span we now do at most a tiny observed-delimiter
// probe and otherwise explicitly open immediately. This increases the chance of
// always returning a visible constrained SMILES span.
// Inside the span, the parser remains the hard authority. In wider parser
// states the strategy uses bounded `ConstrainedSymbolInGenerated` for faster
// multi-token progress; in narrower states it switches to token-level control,
// preferring group-aware constrained decoding early and repetition-penalized
// decoding later to avoid local loops. If EOS is encountered inside a span, the
// strategy first tries a zero-cost rollback repair of the constrained suffix;
// if the repaired prefix is complete it closes, otherwise it exits the loop.
